# Background Remover deliberately does NOT send Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy and
# Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy. Those two headers are what a document needs
# before the browser hands it SharedArrayBuffer, and without SharedArrayBuffer
# ONNX Runtime's WASM build falls back to a single thread no matter how many
# cores the visitor has — so isolating this route is the obvious way to make
# the model faster.
#
# It was tried, and it broke the tool. Once isolation was genuinely in effect
# (an earlier attempt sent each header twice, which browsers reject, so the
# page was never isolated and the slow single-threaded path kept working), the
# runtime took its multi-threaded path and background removal started failing
# outright on real hardware. A slow tool beats a broken one, so the headers are
# off until the threaded path is reproduced and fixed end to end.
#
# If they are restored: exactly ONE rule may match the page. `/tools/background-remover/*`
# already covers the trailing-slash URL; adding `/tools/background-remover/` as
# well makes both rules match, each policy is sent twice, and the joined value
# `same-origin, same-origin` is invalid — the browser then falls back to
# unsafe-none and the page is not isolated at all.
